## Test Category Checklist

### Category 1: Positive Tests (Happy Path)
- [ ] Valid inputs with expected outputs
- [ ] Standard user workflows
- [ ] CRUD operations with valid data
- [ ] Successful authentication/authorization

### Category 2: Negative Tests (Failure Scenarios)
- [ ] Boundary Value Analysis (string lengths, numeric ranges)
- [ ] Invalid data types (alphabetic in numeric fields)
- [ ] Special characters & injection attempts
- [ ] Null reference checks
- [ ] Collection stress (empty, oversized)
- [ ] Date/time paradoxes (future dates, invalid ranges)
- [ ] Dependency failures (database timeout, API errors)

### Category 3: Edge Cases (Boundary Conditions)
- [ ] Financial precision (rounding, zero-sum)
- [ ] Temporal boundaries (fiscal year rollover, leap years)
- [ ] Workflow state machine (illegal transitions)
- [ ] Threshold tests (exact limits, cumulative limits)
- [ ] Globalization (currency formats, multi-byte characters)

### Category 4: Security/Validation Tests
- [ ] SQL Injection prevention
- [ ] XSS (Cross-Site Scripting) prevention
- [ ] IDOR (Insecure Direct Object Reference)
- [ ] Privilege escalation prevention
- [ ] OWASP Top 10 coverage

### Category 5: Concurrency Tests
- [ ] Concurrent updates to same entity
- [ ] Double submit prevention
- [ ] Read during write (transaction isolation)
- [ ] Deadlock scenarios
- [ ] Race conditions in counters/aggregates

---

## Pre-Implementation Checklist

Before implementing tests:
- [ ] All 5 categories included in strategy
- [ ] Test count targets defined for each category
- [ ] OWASP Top 10 coverage planned (if applicable)
- [ ] Negative scenarios cover all error paths
- [ ] Edge cases include boundary values
- [ ] Security tests address injection and authorization
- [ ] Concurrency tests cover race conditions

---

## AI Assistant Workflow

When user requests test creation:

1. ✅ **STOP** - Do not immediately start coding
2. ✅ **CALCULATE** 3:1 ratio requirement first
3. ✅ **CREATE** comprehensive test strategy document
4. ✅ **VERIFY** all 5 categories included with test counts
5. ✅ **DOCUMENT** the 3:1 ratio calculation explicitly
6. ✅ **CONFIRM** with user before implementation
7. ✅ **IMPLEMENT** ALL categories comprehensively

**NEVER**:
- ❌ Implement only positive tests
- ❌ Defer negative/edge tests to "phase 2"
- ❌ Create < 50 tests per negative/edge/security category
- ❌ Create < 25 concurrency tests
- ❌ Proceed if (Negative + Edge) < 3 × Positive

